Description: Run compositor key binds for virtual-keyboard keys
 smithay's zwp_virtual_keyboard_v1 handling sends every key straight to the
 focused client, so an on-screen keyboard (or any input tool built on the
 protocol) can never use a compositor shortcut: Lulo OS's Spotlight,
 Control-F2 menu-bar focus, Control-F3 Dock focus, Command-Tab. niri now
 wraps the per-keyboard dispatch: a key press that matches a configured
 bind runs it and is withheld from the client, along with its release;
 every other request goes to smithay unchanged. Modifiers come from the
 virtual keyboard's own modifiers requests, keysyms from the seat keymap.
 Only unrestricted clients get the virtual keyboard global, as before.
 .
 See ROBOT-13 in docs/parity.md of the rmac repository.
Author: Jacob Samas <samasjacob@icloud.com>
Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-10-14
